      "body": "## Summary\n\nComfyUI's `Flux.forward` (`comfy/ldm/flux/model.py`) passes `ref_latents` (set by the `ReferenceLatent` node, used for FLUX.1 Kontext) and `control` (ControlNet) as named arguments. `FluxAdapter.pack()` in `apps/ComfyUI_SGLDiffusion/executors/flux.py` caught both in `**kwargs` and never forwarded them anywhere. Packing a request with or without these inputs produced an identical request, so a Kontext or ControlNet ComfyUI workflow silently ran as plain text-to-image, with no error.\n\nThe backend `FluxPipeline` has no Kontext/ControlNet support to route these values into (only the Qwen-Image and LongCat paths consume `image_latent`), so implementing full support is out of scope here. Instead of a silent wrong result, `pack()` now raises a clear `ValueError` for either case, matching the existing `ValueError` convention in `adapter.py`'s `get_adapter_class`.\n\n- `control` is confirmed to default to `None` in ComfyUI core (`comfy/samplers.py`: `control = conds.get('control', None)`) and is only non-`None` when a ControlNet node is actually wired into the conditioning, so this cannot false-positive on an ordinary text-to-image workflow.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Added `test_flux_pack_rejects_kontext_reference_latents` and `test_flux_pack_rejects_controlnet_control` to `test/unit/test_comfyui_adapters.py`.\n- Ran `test/unit/test_comfyui_adapters.py` (CPU): 5 passed, including the 2 new regression tests, confirming they fail on the pre-fix adapter and pass on the fix.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37972124324](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37972124324)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37972123657](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37972123657)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37972123802](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37972123802)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
